# C-E14 WebKit list, planned before the start as named acquisitions WK1, WK2, WK3 (each ONE `guarded --exclusive webkit --timeout 90`
# running batch.sh with the start cutoff; chain.sh WK hands each acquisition's .held list to the next unchanged). It cannot fit one 90-minute
# acquisition (P-E14's WK1 + WK2 ran the witnesses alone in about 100 minutes), so the planned split by estimate (P-E14's WebKit stage times;
# C-E13c's for the paths) is: WK1 the attack and the scoring witnesses but E-11; WK2 E-11, the plants, the idle bar beside cand8, the loop,
# the frames and the pass-13 and pass-12 critics' paths; WK3 the pass-11 paths, the older instruments, the paint, cost14 and the exit side
# (M17) behind its load gate. No CDP cell (drag) in WebKit. WebKit retires its browser every 60 page loads (lib.mjs NAV_CAP, tile H3-1).
